{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraphView(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraphView(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraphView(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"metadata":{"title":"SubgraphView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L31","fileName":"SubgraphView.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The kept vertices appear in the base’s order at view indices ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The view keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"renumbered with one array load per entry. A spanning subgraph keeps every vertex at its base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are and, if an edge set was given, when it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices, an edge’s index being its rank"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"count per 64-bit word, and a rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices, except one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that keeps every vertex, which keeps the base’s rows and edge indices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view holds a copy of the base, so mutating the original doesn’t show through. The base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"must have vertex indices; construction traps when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a "},{"code":"GraphAdaptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", its generation is the base’s, and it reads the base’s attached maps."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"[map, of: vertex]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"[map, ofEdgeAt: position]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" trap for a vertex or an edge the view drops,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and their "},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" forms throw. "},{"code":"values(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the base’s, by the base’s positions. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm on the view reads it only at the kept edges."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Subscripts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/Subgraph